    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d375-a3">

                <pb facs="0496" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg428"/>

                <opener>[Enclosure C]</opener>
                <head>Mr. Burlingame to Admiral Bell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 27, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I find that the Chinese government disavows
                    any responsibility for that of Corea, and all jurisdiction over its people.</p>
                <p>Consequently the occurrences there relating to the General Sherman are beyond my
                    jurisdiction. It may, however, strengthen your hands to receive a suggestion
                    from me, that if consistent with your instructions, it may be well to send a
                    vessel of war to inquire into the facts of the case, to the end that they may be
                    reported to the government for its instructions. Having great confidence in your
                    discretion, I leave the matter in your hands, where it prop erly belongs.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ANSON BURLINGAME.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
